# InputPlumber — precompiled aarch64 package pin.
#
# Auto-discovered by rootfs/customize-base.sh (every packages/*/prebuilt.pin is fetched,
# sha256-verified on the host, and extracted into the release base). To add another external
# package not in the holo repo, drop a sibling packages/<name>/prebuilt.pin — no code change.
#
# InputPlumber is NOT in the holo pacman repo, and its .rpm/.deb release assets don't fit
# Arch — so novadeck uses the release's distro-agnostic tarball (rooted at inputplumber/usr,
# hence strip: 1 to land at /usr).
#
# Fields:
#   name     -> staged as work/prebuilt/<name>.tar.gz; also the manifest key
#   url      -> release asset URL (the tarball)
#   sha256   -> from the asset's .sha256.txt sidecar (verified before extract)
#   strip    -> tar --strip-components when extracting into the rootfs
#   deps     -> (optional) space-separated holo-repo packages this prebuilt needs at runtime;
#               pacman-installed into the base alongside it (e.g. shared libraries it links)
#
# To bump: pick a tag at https://github.com/ShadowBlip/InputPlumber/releases and set
# version + url + sha256 together — then re-read the shipped devices/ directory against
# rootfs/overlay/etc/inputplumber/devices.d, because upstream now ships configs for boards we
# also describe. See the note below.
name: inputplumber
version: 0.81.0
url: https://github.com/ShadowBlip/InputPlumber/releases/download/v0.81.0/inputplumber-aarch64.tar.gz
sha256: 5509a6f79bec95c240de34833639e3ba8a144752e3745e6eb978b38b8aa05a10
strip: 1

# 0.78.0 was the release where upstream started describing ARM handhelds at all: it added
# devices/50-ayaneo_pocket_s2.yaml, matching DT `compatible: ayaneo,pocket-s2`, and we deleted our
# own sm8650 description rather than suppress it. A Pocket FIT on 0.78.1 then confirmed upstream's
# reading of that MCU on every point where the two disagreed.
#
# 0.79.0 continued it and covered most of the rest of our roster: 50-ayn_odin2.yaml (matching
# ayn,odin2 AND ayn,odin2portal), 50-ayn_odin2_mini.yaml, 50-ayn_thor.yaml, 50-konkr_pocket_fit.yaml
# and _elite, and 50-retroid_pocket{5,6,_flip2,_mini,_nova}.yaml — plus the capability maps behind
# them: ayn2, ayn3, konkr2, konkr3, ret1, ret2, rsinput1. Every one of our device configs that those
# superseded was deleted with that bump, including our own copy of the Pocket FIT config, which
# shared a FILE NAME with the one upstream ships and so would have won the tie and hidden it.
#
# 0.80.0 TAKES THE AYANEO POCKET DS (upstream bc0fcd4), on the same DT compatible `ayaneo,pocketds`
# and under the same file name ours had — so ours would have won the /etc tie and hidden it, again.
# Ours is deleted with the 0.81.0 bump, and upstream's is NOT a copy of what we had:
#
#   * a hidraw row on 4001:0428 interface 0 — FORCE FEEDBACK, which our description had no row for
#     at all, so rumble on this board was simply absent
#   * `aya10` on the AYANEO-mode pad AND on the AYANEO DEVICE keyboard row, `aya11` on XInput mode,
#     where ours used the generic `dinput_generic` + `aya9`. aya10 is a real board map: analog
#     triggers off ABS_BRAKE/ABS_GAS, the right stick off ABS_Z/ABS_RZ, BTN_START->Guide,
#     BTN6->Start, BTN5->QuickAccess, BTN7->QuickAccess2, and BTN2/BTN_MODE onto the second paddle
#     pair. None of the DS's extra buttons reached Steam under our file.
#
# Two places upstream's DS deliberately differs from ours, and only one of them is a no-op:
#
#   * it drops `maximum_sources: 0`. That is NOT a cap being lifted — unset and any value < 1 both
#     mean unlimited (src/input/manager.rs, the max_sources fallback), so 0 and absent are the same
#     config. Nothing changes.
#   * its XInput row carries NO phys_path, where ours pinned usb-0001:01:00.0-2/input0. Upstream's
#     own Pocket S2 config still pins one; the DS one does not. So on a DS, a REAL external
#     045e:028e pad now matches this 50- config before upstream's 60-xbox_360_gamepad.yaml and gets
#     absorbed into the board's composite device. WATCH FOR THIS the first time a DS is on the
#     bench with an external controller plugged in — and note it has never been exercised end to
#     end anyway, because the DS still has no display (its backlight enable sits behind an on-bus
#     tca6408 expander whose pin is unknown).
#
# Also new in 0.80.0/0.81.0 and free to us: 50-ayn_odin3.yaml (`ayn,odin3`), plus x86 boards we
# don't build for. 50-konkr-fit.yaml is the one that LOOKS like a collision — it sorts before
# 50-konkr_pocket_fit.yaml ('-' < '_') — but it matches on `dmi_data`, so it can never fire on an
# ARM board and our Pocket FIT keeps upstream's devicetree config.
#
# Two upstream fixes in this range are worth knowing when triaging input on hardware: 50263d3
# restores the release delay gamepad macros need, so on-release QuickAccess/Screenshot chords are
# visible to Steam again, and cf93497 restores device-node permissions on unhide and re-triggers
# the udev add.
#
# What upstream still does NOT describe, and what stays in our overlay:
#   * four SM8550 AYANEO Pocket boards — 50-ayaneo_pocket_{ace,dmg,evo,s1}.yaml
#   * the AYN Thor Lite — 50-ayn_thor_lite.yaml, upstream's Retroid description (its `ret1` map, the
#     same driver, the same 2020:3001 MCU) behind a DT `model` match, because its `compatible`
#     `ayn,thor-lite` is not what upstream's 50-ayn_thor.yaml keys on
#   * the MANGMI Pocket Max — 50-mangmi_pocket_max.yaml plus our sm8250_pocket_max_mcu map; its pad
#     is an SPI MCU on a driver nothing else uses, so there is nothing upstream to adopt
#
# Binary links libiio.so.0 (IIO sensors/gyro) — pulled from the holo repo, not bundled.
# Re-read on the 0.81.0 bump: still the only non-base NEEDED entry (libudev, libgcc_s, libm, libc
# are all base).
deps: libiio
